    "title": "Cody Johnson makes RodeoHouston history",
    "text": "The country star sells out NRG Stadium and RodeoHouston’s final nightCody Johnson closed out the 94th Houston Livestock Show and Rodeo in historic fashion Sunday night (Mar 22nd), drawing the largest crowd ever at NRG Stadium and RodeoHouston history. CoJo surpassed the legendary “concert-only” attendance record of 80,020 set by George Strait in 2013, with 80,203 to end the 2026 edition. “Tonight is the most incredible night in my career, so far. You guys and myself have sold out the Rodeo. It’s the largest crowd ever in NRG Stadium and HoustonRodeo’s history, so thank you!” he says in a video posted ahead of his performance. Johnson is a Texas native and multi-platinum country music artist who has performed at RodeoHouston five times: 2017, 2018, 2019, 2022, and 2023. His song “Welcome to the Show” debuted in 2019 and was written and recorded to serve as RodeoHouston’s official theme song. Since 2017, Johnson has become a fan favorite with his unforgettable presence on the star stage. His 2023 performance welcomed more than 73,000 fans, and in 2022, he drew more than 70,500. On March 6, 2024, Johnson surprised Rodeo guests during Jelly Roll’s performance.This is the fourth full-length concert at the Houston Livestock Show and Rodeo, following Strait in 2013 and 2022, and Garth Brooks in 2018.Johnson is among the first round of performers set for the 61st ACM Awards on May 17th, on Prime Video. He joins Lainey Wilson and Riley Green, with additional unforgettable performances to be announced in the coming weeks.",
